# Cloudflare Pages custom headers

# CMS-uploaded images live at a stable, un-fingerprinted path. Before an image is
# deployed, a request to its URL returns a 200 HTML fallback that Cloudflare tags with
# `max-age=14400` (4 hours). When the editor previews an article in /admin/ the image
# does not exist yet, so the browser caches that fallback and shows a broken image until
# a hard refresh. Force revalidation on this path so freshly published images load
# immediately (unchanged images still return a cheap 304 via ETag).
/images/uploads/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
